{
  "_comment": "Canonical model catalogue — single source of truth for the models offered by document generation AND RAG chat. Loaded by MCP (model_strategies.catalogue). The RAG backend routes by parsing the provider/model id and does not read this file; provider client construction stays in code (per-service adapters). 'credential_env' lists env vars any of which, when set, make a cloud model available; local models need none. 'rag_capable' marks models the RAG chat surface may offer (excludes doc-gen-only mechanisms like claude-cli, defined in code). Entries are verified against each provider's live /models endpoint, not written from memory: a catalogue id the provider no longer serves fails at generation time, not at startup.",
